    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.46.0 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. Only the pegasus artifact changed: install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.28.0 and earlier. v5.46.0 reaches this distribution through the instructions its agents carry, and every change in it shares one root -- a guard, or an instruction, approving by the name of a thing instead of by the thing itself. Compression is now stated as a property of what comes back, never of the brief that goes out. The delegation criterion preached compression in eight separate lines, all of them about the child's report, and said nothing at all about how to write a brief. The cost was observed live: briefs and memory writes arrived with their grammar destroyed, words fused to save tokens, and an executor invented requirements nobody had asked for which then became gates a person had to withdraw explicitly. What you leave out, the executor invents, and an invented requirement is a gate someone must negotiate down -- the exact cost compression exists to avoid. The orchestrator's own rule already held the right principle, that a brief needing interpretation before it can be obeyed has failed, but it enumerated only the warm failures: persona, slang, capitals. It now names both extremes as one failure. RED stopped being declared and became observed. The Strict-TDD evidence column was defined as always reading the same fixed value, which cannot distinguish a task that wrote its test first from one that did not, and the RED step never executed anything -- the protocol said failure was guaranteed so confirming it was unnecessary, while GREEN three lines below did require a run. Verification checked only that the fixed string was present and the test file existed, both true regardless of the order the code was written in. Two consecutive changes therefore reached the end with evidence that could not be reconstructed, and the only exit was a signed exception. RED is now run and observed before production code exists, and the cell records the command and the failure it produced. Two distinctions the real session made explicit are written down: a blanket missing-symbol failure is a legitimate RED for the task introducing that symbol but does not individually prove the scenarios it masks, and a failure caused by a broken fixture or environment is not a RED at all. What one side must record and what the other must check are defined once and checked against both files, so a verifier can never again demand evidence the implementing phase was never asked to produce. Two guards that measured a label now measure the thing. An implementing phase reported splitting its tests into three scenario groups and running each; verification found the selectors changed the names printed in the output, not the tests executed -- one group running three times under three labels, a report true about its labels and false about its work. The verification craft now orders resolving every claimed group to the command or selector it actually ran, and crediting only the first execution when two resolve to the same selection. Separately, the three budgets limiting how much text a prompt carries counted lines, and that was proven purchasable by reformatting: collapsing a hand-wrapped bullet while also adding prose took a file from 103 lines to 101 while it gained 48 words, and the guard named for trading text for text passed while text was added and none removed. They now count words, which no reflow can buy, each ceiling deriving its headroom from the proportion its retired line ceiling had when it was created. That property is demonstrated rather than asserted: a guard rewraps the real body and requires the count not to move. This distribution changed nothing of its own for this pin beyond the alignment."
